    "known": "strong",
    "summary": "Four recently deceased humans wake in a pastel afterlife neighborhood and are told they are in the Good Place. Eleanor Shellstrop, a selfish saleswoman, is sure she was sent by mistake and persuades her assigned soulmate, ethics professor Chidi Anagonye, to teach her to be good. The neighborhood is actually a Bad Place torture experiment run by the demon Michael, and Eleanor figures this out in the season one finale. Over subsequent seasons the group escapes, goes to Earth to prove they can improve, and eventually confronts the flawed points system that condemns nearly everyone. They persuade the Judge to replace eternal punishment with a test-and-rehabilitation system, enter the real Good Place, and discover that even paradise becomes unbearable without an end. ||They institute a door out of existence, and each main character eventually walks through it after long, varied afterlives.||",
